[47.815531, "o", "` Python package files (the actual `pip/` module directory) were missing from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`. Only the metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info`) remained, which is why Python reported pip as \"already installed\" but couldn't import it.\r\n\r\n**What I did:** Removed the stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which extracted the bundled `pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl` into site-packages. pip is now working and can install packages.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=27 surface=2f77a83e3748\r\n"]
